<Layout title="Restored Beauty Coaching">
  <Logo slot="hero" class="max-w-150" />

  <H1 class="text-center">Restored Beauty Coaching</H1>

  <H2>Contact</H2>
  <P>
    I'm currently accepting virtual appointments for individual clients. Email
    me for a free consultation.
  </P>

  <P
    ><b>Email: </b>
    <a href="mailto:andrea@restoredbeautycoaching.com" class="text-blue-500"
      >andrea@restoredbeautycoaching.com</a
    ></P
  >

  <H2>What is Story Work?</H2>

  <P>
    We are shaped by the experiences, places, and people that surrounded us as
    we grew. Some memories shine bright and clear; others stay hidden, tucked
    away beneath the surface. When we craft these moments into concrete stories,
    we begin a journey of understanding ourselves more deeply. Story work helps
    us see how our past has shaped who we are today. Sharing our stories lets us
    see ourselves with fresh eyes. It helps us understand what has held us back
    from loving fully, reconnect with parts of ourselves we may have lost, and
    live with more purpose. Many of us carry pain from the past moments when we
    didn’t have the words or safe space to express what we felt. These hidden
    wounds often bring shame and keep us stuck. When we tell our stories in a
    caring, supportive space, healing can begin. We find the strength to face
    our pain, speak our truths, and let go of shame. Through this, we open the
    door to freedom and hope.
  </P>

  <H2> Individual Story Work </H2>

  <P>
    Individual story work is a one-on-one, trauma-informed practice that
    explores the experiences, relationships, and environments that have shaped
    your life. Some stories are easy to remember, others remain hidden in your
    body and heart, but all influence how you live, love, and understand
    yourself.
  </P>

  <P>
    In a safe, supportive space, you are invited to name and explore your story
    at your own pace. This process can help you:
  </P>

  <Ul>
    <li>
      Understand patterns that affect your relationships and sense of self
    </li>
    <li>Reconnect with parts of yourself that have been hidden or silenced</li>
    <li>Engage experiences of harm or trauma with care</li>
    <li>Loosen shame and self-criticism</li>
    <li>Live with greater freedom, purpose, and presence</li>
  </Ul>

  <P>
    This work is not about fixing or problem-solving. It is about being known
    and accompanying your story with compassion.
  </P>

  <H2> What to Expect </H2>

  <Ul>
    <li>
      <b>Safe, attuned relationship:</b> You are met with care, curiosity, and consistency.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Pacing that honors your nervous system:</b> You remain in control of what
      you share and when.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Exploring your story intentionally:</b> We notice patterns, formative experiences,
      and survival strategies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Engaging trauma with care:</b> Healing comes from being seen and held, not
      forced disclosure.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Integration, not quick fixes:</b> Over time, story work can foster clarity,
      self-compassion, and connection.
    </li>
  </Ul>

  <H2>Is Story Work Right for Me?</H2>

  <P>Story work may be helpful if you:</P>
  <Ul>
    <li>
      Feel stuck in patterns or emotional responses you don’t fully understand
    </li>
    <li>Carry shame, self-criticism, or disconnection</li>
    <li>Want to explore your story with curiosity and compassion</li>
    <li>Desire relational, slow-paced support for healing</li>
  </Ul>

  <P
    >It may <b>not</b> be right if you are looking for immediate solutions or directives.
    Story work complements therapy but does not replace it.</P
  >

  <P
    ><b>Disclaimer:</b> Individual story work is a reflective, relational practice.
    It is not a substitute for mental health therapy or medical care. If you are
    experiencing crisis or acute mental health challenges, seek support from a licensed
    professional.</P
  >

